{
    "background_story": "Champ was a majestic stallion with a shiny black coat and a proud demeanor. He lived on a sprawling estate owned by a wealthy prebendary, a high-ranking clergyman in the local church. The prebendary, known for his love of horses, had hand-picked Champ from a prestigious breeding farm. As the prebendary's favorite mount, Champ would often accompany him on ceremonial rides through the countryside, drawing admiring glances from the villagers. Despite his regal bearing, Champ had a gentle soul and was beloved by the estate's staff, who spoiled him with treats and affection. On Sundays, Champ would proudly carry the prebendary to church, where he would wait patiently outside, a symbol of the prebendary's status and Champ's own noble spirit.",
